  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Starting**: The player with the highest double leads. This double is the 'Spinner'. 2. **Individual Arms**: Each player has an 'arm' extending from the spinner. You can normally only play on your own arm. 3. **Opening an Arm**: If you cannot play a tile, you must 'Open' your arm (often marked with a coin). 4. **Public Access**: Any player can play on an 'Open' arm. The owner of the arm 'Closes' it as soon as they are able to make a play on it again. 5. **Doubles**: Doubles are played sideways and do not branch (traditional Cuban style).",
    Player: "1. **Starting**: The player with the highest double leads. This double is the 'Spinner'. 2. **Individual Arms**: Each player has an 'arm' extending from the spinner. You can normally only play on your own arm. 3. **Opening an Arm**: If you cannot play a tile, you must 'Open' your arm (often marked with a coin). 4. **Public Access**: Any player can play on an 'Open' arm. The owner of the arm 'Closes' it as soon as they are able to make a play on it again. 5. **Doubles**: Doubles are played sideways and do not branch (traditional Cuban style).",
    objective: 'Be the first to play all tiles (Domino!) or have the lowest pip-count when the game is blocked. 100 points wins.',
    gameplay: "1. **Starting**: The player with the highest double leads. This double is the 'Spinner'. 2. **Individual Arms**: Each player has an 'arm' extending from the spinner. You can normally only play on your own arm. 3. **Opening an Arm**: If you cannot play a tile, you must 'Open' your arm (often marked with a coin). 4. **Public Access**: Any player can play on an 'Open' arm. The owner of the arm 'Closes' it as soon as they are able to make a play on it again. 5. **Doubles**: Doubles are played sideways and do not branch (traditional Cuban style).",
    keyRules: [
      'Highest double leads and becomes the Spinner.',
      'Each player has their own arm extending from the spinner.',
      'Can normally only play on your own arm.',
      "If cannot play, must 'Open' your armâ€”others can then play on it.",
      "Owner 'Closes' arm when they play on it again.",
      "Winner scores total pips in opponents' hands.",
      'First to 100 points wins.',
