      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Starting**: The player with the highest double leads. This double is the 'Spinner'. 2. **Individual Arms**: Each player has an 'arm' extending from the spinner. You can normally only play on your own arm. 3. **Opening an Arm**: If you cannot play a tile, you must 'Open' your arm (often marked with a coin). 4. **Public Access**: Any player can play on an 'Open' arm. The owner of the arm 'Closes' it as soon as they are able to make a play on it again. 5. **Doubles**: Doubles are played sideways and do not branch (traditional Cuban style).",
